WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:07.620
(Electronic music)

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.740
- (Jared) What’s up Wisecrack, Jared here
to talk about the show with the best fans

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:14.959
on the internet, Rick and Morty. Now the most
recent episode is one of our favorite of the

00:00:14.959 --> 00:00:17.730
season so far. I mean, it’s got wet eggs:

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:20.289
- (Morty) I told you not to look at that egg,
it was too wet!

00:00:20.289 --> 00:00:23.609
- (Jared) And well, uh… you know

00:00:23.609 --> 00:00:25.829
- (Rick) Honestly I’m proud of us for not…

00:00:25.829 --> 00:00:29.369
- (Jared) But what we found most interesting
about this episode is the basic question it

00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:32.629
poses: how much should nature define us?

00:00:32.629 --> 00:00:37.160
Welcome to this Wisecrack Quicktake on Rick
and Morty Season 4 Episode 7: Promorteus

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.000
And duh… spoilers ahead.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:41.520
So the basic premise of Promorteus is this:
there’s a parasitic, face-hugging alien

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:46.470
species that exerts total control of their
host and, has a life span of about 30 minutes.

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:51.409
After depositing an egg, said host explodes,
killing itself and the proud parasite mommy

00:01:51.409 --> 00:01:54.189
- (Alien) Suck on face, sh** an egg, and die!

00:01:54.189 --> 00:01:59.000
- (Jared) But Summer, using a fool-proof oral
defense mechanism, escapes enslavement and

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:04.920
convinces the parasites to forego their reproductive
urges to live a longer, more fulfilling life.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:09.679
As a result, the parasites are able to quickly
build a sprawling society with media, matching

00:02:09.679 --> 00:02:15.090
skyscrapers, and pearl harbors. And then of
course, Rick blows it all up - minus the twin

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:16.170
skyscrapers, of course.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:19.590
- (Morty) Totally would’ve been cheap
- (Rick) Yeah real low hanging fruit, we’re

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:20.590
better than that.

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:21.840
- (Jared) Also Jerry has bees.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:26.760
I think one of the most interesting elements
of this episode lies in this small gag: Parasite

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:31.689
Rick Glorzo-tube rants against the progressive
agenda of living longer. Now, at first, this

00:02:31.689 --> 00:02:33.860
seems like a a quick jab at people like Alex
Jones

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:36.810
- (Parasite Rick) Did I least sell out and
sell vitamins or something?

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:41.129
- (Jared) But the basic concept is mirrored
everywhere in the episode. That is: if something

00:02:41.129 --> 00:02:44.050
is natural, does that make it right?

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:48.599
Face-hugger Rick’s argument for the murder/suicide
of host and parasite is based on quote unquote

00:02:48.599 --> 00:02:49.599
science

00:02:49.599 --> 00:02:54.019
- (Parasite Rick) Here's a scientific fact
I'm not “allowed to say" - our hosts are

00:02:54.019 --> 00:02:58.599
biologically designed to incubate your eggs...
if that triggers you, f*** off!

00:02:58.599 --> 00:03:02.750
- (Jared) Of course, this is not actually
science, it’s the mention of science in

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:06.239
a logical fallacy: the appeal to nature fallacy.

00:03:06.239 --> 00:03:10.829
That is, the idea that if something is natural,
it is inherently good, desirable, or even

00:03:10.829 --> 00:03:16.040
inevitable. This kind of fallacy pops up everywhere.
In the debate about same-sex marriage, many

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:20.950
people would argue that homosexuality was
unnatural, and therefore immoral. Then again,

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:25.819
getting mauled by a tiger IS perfectly natural,
but that doesn’t mean it’s good. This

00:03:25.819 --> 00:03:31.230
the appeal to nature fallacy in action. Others
would point to the fact, correctly, that homosexuality

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:36.090
is natural among many of our closest animal
relatives - which again, is still a logical

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:40.129
fallacy, since dictating where you can or
can’t stick your genitals based on what

00:03:40.129 --> 00:03:43.580
does or doesn’t happen in nature is a logical
fallacy.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:47.480
This fallacy also pops up often around the
idea that “might is right,” the idea that

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:52.099
people are justified to rule by strength alone.
That claim usually gets backed up by citing

00:03:52.099 --> 00:03:56.799
Darwinism, whatever primates do or don’t
do in the wild, or our evolutionary history

00:03:56.799 --> 00:04:00.749
of humans being dicks. Pretty much, every
time you hear about monkeys, primates, or

00:04:00.749 --> 00:04:05.819
our cave-men ancestors, you should stop listening
to that person. Except that’s a fallacy

00:04:05.819 --> 00:04:11.310
fallacy, dismissing a conclusion outright
because its logic was flawed - ****. Anyway.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.349
Everyone shut up about monkeys already.

00:04:13.349 --> 00:04:16.980
Parasite Rick’s argument is exactly this
kind of appeal to nature. , He says “we

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:20.610
should deposit our eggs because the hosts
can biologically sustain them”. He also

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:25.600
has a poster on his wall that displays a kind
of might-is-right logic, reading that “Glorzo’s

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:30.190
are supreme,” and hosts are subservient,
which echoes plenty of bad appeals to nature

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:34.220
found in places like social darwinism. The
progress of Summer on the other hand, is about

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:36.660
moving past biology determining one’s future

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:40.260
- (Parasite Morty) Let’s just get the hell
out of here and be whatever the fuck we want,

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:42.420
that’s evolution, that’s progress!

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:46.421
- (Jared) But there’s also a more subtle
critique going on here. Important to this

00:04:46.421 --> 00:04:51.780
episode, and life, is that people, when appealing
to nature, often set up an arbitrary divide

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:53.720
between good nature and bad nature.

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:56.970
- (Parasite Rick) F*** since we were in eggs?
Oh yeah yeah yeah, what, now you respect like

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:59.620
the biological institutions now? F*** you!

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:03.840
- (Jared) People arguing that same-sex marriage
is bad because it’s unnatural usually have

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:08.530
no problem watching YouTube for 8-hours a
day, getting blood transfusions, or being

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:11.590
temperature regulated by the liquid remains
of dinosaurs.

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:18.060
Similarly, Parasite Rick has no problem enjoying
the unnatural spoils of civilization or non-reproductive,

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:23.130
arguably incestual, face-sucking while railing
against the repression of biological processes

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:25.639
- (Parasite Morty) How come you haven’t
laid an egg inside this old man yet?

00:05:25.639 --> 00:05:27.180
- (Parasite Rick) Because I do what I want!

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:30.780
- (Jared) Similarly, one could “respect
nature” while “despising” parts of it

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:35.690
that seem icky or just dangerous. Like snakes
which have historically been labeled in some

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:36.889
cultures as evil incarnate.

00:05:36.889 --> 00:05:37.889
- (Morty) What is that?
- (Tick) Obviously it’s a space snake.

00:05:37.889 --> 00:05:38.889
- (Morty) There’s snakes in space?

00:05:38.889 --> 00:05:40.910
- (Jared) And of course, there’s parasites,
which, to my knowledge, don’t really have

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:44.760
too many positive representations in the media
. It’s pretty much a default to think of

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:45.760
them as a mindless

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:48.535
- (Rick) They're face-hugging parasites I
don't think their society is going to be that

00:05:48.535 --> 00:05:49.535
difficult to navigate

00:05:49.535 --> 00:05:50.535
- (Jared) And evil

00:05:50.535 --> 00:05:52.259
- (Morty) I’m sorry we thought you were
evil!

00:05:52.259 --> 00:05:56.970
- (Alien) Why would you think that? We had
a giant tower blared Glorzo is peace!

00:05:56.970 --> 00:05:58.910
- (Morty) I know, I should, should, should
we help?

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:02.580
- (Jared) But here’s where the episode gets
really interesting, because this looking down

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:07.880
on our face-huggers is, in a weird way, a
mirror image of Parasite Rick. Normal Rick

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:13.150
views parasites as lowly, a lesser form of
life. As Rick and Morty commit mass murder

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:16.340
they note how good is feels to cause mayhem
without guilt.

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:18.440
- (Rick) Damn feels kind of good when there’s
no guilt

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:21.389
- (Morty) Yeah it’s just like in Star Wars
- (Rick) Yeah just like in Star Wars

00:06:21.389 --> 00:06:24.500
- (Jared) Comparing it to popping bubble wrap
- not destroying an advanced civilization.

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:27.390
- (Rick) Oh my god this is so much fun!
- (Morty) I don’t want to stop!

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:28.720
- (Rick) Yeah it’s like popping bubblewrap!

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:33.070
- (Jared) But this idea is constantly undercut
as the show likens Rick and Morty’s violence

00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:34.070
to American tragedies

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:38.450
- (Beth) So you did a 9/11?
- (Morty) Almost did a 9/11, we, we went with

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:42.720
a Pearl Harbor. We’re pretty classy.
- (Beth) Why were either of those two an option?

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:43.770
- (Jared) Morty even comments:

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:45.710
- (Morty) Should have been a better species!

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:49.460
- (Jared) echoing might-is-right justification
for destroying their world before becoming

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:51.449
horrified by his actions.

00:06:51.449 --> 00:06:53.310
- (Morty) Sorry. I’m sorry!

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:57.310
- (Jared) It’s not all that different than
Parasite Rick’s justification for enslaving

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:02.520
host species - humans killing parasites is
just some old-fashioned natural pest control,

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:04.590
even if by some unnatural means.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:09.300
There’s also just a really interesting question
here that I love. There’s a basic hypothetical:

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:13.920
Is it fair to call a species evil for just
reproducing as their nature dictates? What

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:18.140
would happen if we encountered an intelligent
alien that could only survive by living parasitically

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:23.150
off another sentient alien? Is there even
a line in the sand we can draw, as a species

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:27.250
that lives off of eating other species? Just
some FOOD for thought.

